[Options]
; mpv.jcf -- the JAWS configuration file for mpv.
;
; DELIBERATELY ALMOST EMPTY, AND PRESENT ON PURPOSE.
;
; Nothing here changes a setting. The file exists so that JAWS treats mpv as an
; application it knows about rather than an unknown one, which is the difference
; between the mpv scripts loading and not.
;
; The evidence for that: in the JAWS settings folder, EVERY application with
; working scripts has one of these beside them -- chrome, cmd, edsharp, excel,
; firefox, notepad, and FileDir itself. mpv had scripts, a key map and a
; compiled .jsb, and no .jcf, and JAWS answered "the application currently
; being used is mpv.exe" and "default settings are loaded" in the same breath.
;
; A section header with no settings under it is a valid configuration: JAWS
; takes its default for everything unnamed, which is what is wanted. This file
; is here to be found, not to change behaviour.
